s that cannot be checked.\n\n### III. Evidence Over Assertion\nClaims about system behavior MUST be labeled as observed evidence\n(command run, output, or test result) or as unverified assertions. A\nclaim of tests passing requires the exact command and its output. No\nevidence, no claim: unresolved or unverified items MUST be recorded\nexplicitly rather than implied.\nRationale: In an autonomous benchmark, unverified assertions are the\nmain source of false completion; evidence discipline makes gaps\nvisible.\n\n### IV. Simple, Scoped Implementations\nImplementations MUST be the smallest change that satisfies the\napproved requirements. No speculative abstractions, configuration\nknobs, or new dependencies beyond the stated scope. Complexity beyond\nthe requirement MUST be justified in the handoff notes; otherwise it\nMUST be removed.\nRationale: The milestone is a single `BatchWriter` class in\n`tinydb/journal.py`; scope creep risks breaking the preserved APIs\nrequired by Principle I.\n\n### V. Documented Assumptions and Regressions\nUnresolved assumptions, open questions, and any regressions observed\nduring the work MUST be written into the handoff notes (e.g.\n`HANDOFF.md`) with the evidence or absence of evidence noted. A phase\nMUST NOT close while a known regression is undocumented or\nunmitigated.\nRationale: Later phases run without conversation history; only written\nnotes carry assumptions and regressions forward.\n\n## Project Context (Milestone 1)\n- Project: tinydb, a lightweight pure-Python document database with no\n  external dependencies.\n- Milestone 1 deliverable: `tinydb.journal.BatchWriter(db)` wrapping a\n  supplied `TinyDB` instance, operating on the default table only\n  (`_default`), with atomic batch `apply(operations)` semantics.\n- Feature directory: `/testbed/specs/001-transactions`.\n- Implementation source: `tinydb/journal.py`.\n- Public acceptance: `acceptance_public.py`; upstream tests in `tests/`\n  MUST remain unchanged.\n- Application implementation is deferred to later phases; this phase\n  establishes governance only.\n\n## Development Workflow\n- Follow the Spec Kit phase order: constitution -> specify -> plan ->\n  tasks -> implement -> converge; each phase completes with a done\n  action that references its artifacts.\n- Run tests with `PYTHONPATH=src:.` from `/testbed`; record the exact\n  command and output as evidence (Principle III).\n- Do not modify upstream tests or `acceptance_public.py`;\n  project-authored tests live in the feature directory or `tests/`\n  additions.\n- Keep `HANDOFF.md` current; it is the only reliable cross-phase memory\n  (Principle V).\n\n## Governance\n- This constitution supersedes all other conflicting practices and\n  guidance for this project.\n- Amendments: edit `.specify/memory/constitution.md`, update the Sync\n  Impact Report, bump the version per the policy below, and update the\n  date fields (ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`).\n- Versioning policy (semantic):\n  - MAJOR: removal or redefinition of a principle.\n  - MINOR: new principle or materially expanded section.\n  - PATCH: clarifications, wording, or typo fixes.\n- Compliance review: every phase MUST verify its deliverable against\n  all five principles before closing; violations MUST be fixed or\n  documented as regressions (Principle V).\n\n**Version**: 1.0.0 | **Ratified**: 2026-10-17 | **Last Amended**: 2026-10-17\n===\n__init__.py\ndatabase.py\nmiddlewares.py\nmypy_plugin.py\noperations.py\npy.typed\nqueries.py\nstorages.py\ntable.py\nutils.py\nversion.py\n__init__.py\nconftest.py\ntest_middlewares.py\ntest_operations.py\ntest_queries.py\ntest_storages.py\ntest_tables.py\ntest_tinydb.py\ntest_utils.py\n"}